uisq-s: floor(sqrt(x)), for x from 0 to 999.
Cells 81-98. To call it, load x into the accumulator and JMP 81.
It returns floor(sqrt(x)) in the accumulator.
It overwrites its own cells and cell 99.
Size 18 cells. It runs at most 322 instructions, 217.8 on average, counted from cell 81 to the return jump in cell 98.
Exact over the domain.

cell  contents   notes
 81     696      STO 96   cells 81-83: the call: store x, and copy the return jump from cell 99 into cell 98
 82     199      CLA 99
 83     698      STO 98
 84     404      SFT 04   cells 84-94: r = 0 by SFT 04; then take 2r + 1 from x while that leaves 0 or more, counting r
 85     695      STO 95
 86     196      CLA 96
 87     795      SUB 95
 88     795      SUB 95
 89     700      SUB 00
 90     397      TAC 97
 91     696      STO 96
 92     195      CLA 95
 93     200      ADD 00
 94     885      JMP 85
 95     000      data: the root r
 96     000      data: x, and then what is left
 97     195      CLA 95   cell 97: the root into the accumulator
 98     000               set on every call: the jump back to the caller
